@page
@model SetupAndDeployModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Setup and deploy";
    ViewData[GuidanceNavigation.SectionViewDataKey] = GuidanceNavigation.SetupAndDeploy;
}

@section SideNav {
    @await Html.PartialAsync("_GuidanceSideNav")
}

<div class="dfe-c-fe-shell">
    <header class="dfe-c-fe-page-header">
        <div class="dfe-c-fe-page-header__intro">
            <p class="dfe-c-fe-eyebrow">User guide</p>
            <h1 class="dfe-c-fe-title">Setup and deploy</h1>
            <p class="dfe-c-fe-text govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
                After you create or host, Prototype Manager provisions GitHub and Azure in the background, then wires up deployment.
            </p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Setup progress</h2>
    <p class="govuk-body">
        The setup page lists each step as Completed, In progress, or Failed. Steps run as background jobs — you don’t need to keep the browser open, but staying on the page shows live updates.
    </p>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>for a new prototype this usually includes creating the GitHub repo, adding the Prototype Kit, and creating Azure hosting</li>
        <li>failed steps can be retried without starting over</li>
        <li>when hosting is ready you may get an email with the URL, password, and next steps (if Notify is configured)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m govuk-!-margin-top-6">Deploy</h2>
    <p class="govuk-body">
        On the prototype’s <strong>Deploy</strong> tab you can see the GitHub repository and Azure resources, and configure automated deployment.
    </p>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Prototype Manager can commit a GitHub Actions workflow and store the Azure publish profile as a repository secret</li>
        <li>it can trigger the first deployment for you</li>
        <li>after that, pushes to <code>main</code> deploy updates automatically</li>
        <li>if configuration fails, check the job status and error message on Deploy or Activity</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="govuk-body">
        Deployment is often queued automatically once hosting succeeds. Use Deploy to retry or re-run configuration if something went wrong.
    </p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m govuk-!-margin-top-6">If a step fails</h2>
    <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
        <li>Read the error on the setup or Deploy page — many failures are permission or naming issues.</li>
        <li>Retry the failed step from the same screen.</li>
        <li>If it keeps failing, email DesignOps with the prototype name and error text.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="govuk-inset-text">
        <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
            For how jobs and the GitHub App work under the hood, see
            <a class="govuk-link" href="@Url.Page("/Guidance/Technical/GitHub")">GitHub integration</a>
            and
            <a class="govuk-link" href="@Url.Page("/Guidance/Technical/Operations")">Jobs and access</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
